# Level 0 → 1 — READING A FILE IN THE HOME DIRECTORY


## LEVEL GOAL
Find and read the password stored in a file called `readme` in the home directory.

## DESCRIPTION
This level introduces two fundamental Linux commands: `ls` (list directory contents) and `cat` (display file contents).

## APPROACH
After logging in, I listed the home directory contents:

```bash
ls
```

The `readme` file was present. I read it with:

```bash
cat readme
```

The file contained a welcome message followed by the password.

> Password obtained. [Not shared per OverTheWire rules]

## KEY TAKEAWAY
Every subsequent level follows this same pattern — locate, then read. `ls` and `cat` are the starting point for nearly every Linux investigation.
